{"type":"text","timestamp":1788505383940,"sessionID":"ses_f94ccbbd8ffex6r1tm6ai3wHOS","part":{"id":"prt_06b3a4bc80015XtJ7lCnwn9PSe","messageID":"msg_06b3a305e001DKHiNmGio5dZ2w","sessionID":"ses_f94ccbbd8ffex6r1tm6ai3wHOS","type":"text","text":"`extra_args` support is implemented:\n\n**Changes**\n- `src/agents/model_settings.py:76` — New `extra_args: dict[str, Any] | None` field with docstring documentation and cautionary notes (auto-appears in the API reference via mkdocstrings). `resolve()` now **merges** `extra_args` from base and override settings, with override keys taking precedence on conflicts; originals are never mutated.\n- `src/agents/models/openai_chatcompletions.py:287` — Extra args are passed via `**` to `chat.completions.create` (non-streaming and streaming).\n- `src/agents/models/openai_responses.py:272` — Same passthrough to `responses.create`.\n- `src/agents/extensions/models/litellm_model.py:286` — Merged into litellm's `acompletion` kwargs.\n\n**Behavior**\n- None values are automatically filtered out before any API call.\n- No `extra_args` (or empty dict) → nothing extra is added to the call.\n- Works alongside all existing settings (`temperature`, `extra_body`, `extra_headers`, etc.).\n\n**Tests** (`tests/test_extra_args.py`, plus serialization coverage)\n- Passthrough to both Responses and ChatCompletions models\n- None-value filtering for both models\n- No-op when unset\n- `resolve()` merging with override precedence, missing-dict handling, and no-mutation guarantees\n\n**Verification**: `ruff format`/`check` clean, `mypy` clean on touched files (remaining errors are pre-existing missing stubs for litellm/numpy/mcp), full suite shows zero new failures (the 9 failures are pre-existing environment issues present on the baseline).","time":{"start":1788505377736,"end":1788505383935}}}
